Personnel records are stored in the shared NAHPU database and can be assigned
to multiple projects. Each project shows only the personnel assigned to it.

## Adding personnel to a project

{% aside type="caution" %}

`Personnel` Field IDs require a `Cataloger` with a registered personal field
number. `Project` Field IDs use the project numbering convention instead.
Choose the role carefully: once a person is saved as a `Cataloger`, that role
cannot be changed.

{% /aside %}

From the `Personnel` panel on the project dashboard, select `Add personnel`:

- If people already exist in the database, choose `Select from database` {% ref id="E" /%}
  (`Select existing` on narrow screens) to pick and assign
  them, or switch to `Add new personnel` {% ref id="F" /%} (`Add new` on narrow
  screens) to create someone new.
- If the database has no personnel yet, the new-person form opens directly.

| Field | Shown | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Name*` {% ref id="G" /%} | Always | Required. |
| Photo | Always | Optional avatar or portrait. |
| `Affiliation` | Always | The person's institution. |
| `ORCID iD` | Always | Optional, hyphenated, with a valid checksum (for example, `0000-0002-1825-0097`). |
| `Specimen care role` {% ref id="B" /%} | Always | `Cataloger`, `Preparator only`, `Determiner only`, or `None`. |
| `Email` | After `Show more` {% ref id="H" /%} | Saved in lowercase when adding a new person. |
| `Phone` | After `Show more` | Digits only. |
| `Notes` | After `Show more` | Additional notes about the person. |

When editing an existing person, the `Contact` and `Notes` sections start
expanded. In Darwin Core exports, NAHPU uses the canonical
`https://orcid.org/...` URL as the agent identifier when an `ORCID iD` is
present, and falls back to the NAHPU personnel UUID otherwise.

## Field numbers for catalogers

When `Specimen care role` is `Cataloger`, NAHPU shows `Register personal field
number` {% ref id="C" /%}. Turn it on when that cataloger's initials and
running number should generate specimen `Field ID` values:

- **`Initials*`**: 2–5 characters (letters, digits, `-`, or `_`), saved in
  capitals.
- **`Cataloger number*`**: starting integer; advances automatically as
  specimens are created.

Field-number registration is optional. If your collection uses project-based
numbering, configure `Project` Field IDs in [Settings](../settings/#field-id)
instead of creating a fictitious person for the project code.

## Editing and removing personnel

- **Edit in a project**: select the edit icon beside a person in the dashboard
  `Personnel` panel.
- **Remove from a project**: select `Select` in the dashboard `Personnel`
  panel, check the people to remove, and choose `Remove N personnel from
  project`. Removing someone from a project keeps their shared database record.
  A person cannot be removed while project records still reference them.
- **Manage all database personnel**: select `Manage` in the dashboard
  `Personnel` panel or open `Settings` > `Database` > `Personnel` to open
  `Manage personnel` {% ref id="A" /%}. Search or inspect details, choose
  `Edit personnel` {% ref id="D" /%} to update a record, or use `Select` to
  permanently delete people who are not assigned to any project (assigned
  people are protected and cannot be selected).

## Terminology

### Cataloger

Creates and edits specimen catalog records, and can appear in cataloger,
preparator, and collecting-personnel fields. The `Cataloger` role cannot be
changed after saving; other roles can be edited.

### Preparator only

Helps prepare specimens without creating or editing catalog records.

### Determiner only

Identifies specimens without cataloging or preparing them. Appears in the
specimen form's `Determiner` field.

### None

Supports fieldwork without a specimen-care role (such as a guide, driver, or
cook). Can still be recorded as collecting personnel on events.
